(version 1)
# Custom DRC rules (2026-09-08; SMD board = 0.4 / 0.6 mm): routing hygiene by IMPEDANCE, on top of the net classes
# (Default = low-Z signal 0.5 mm, HiZ = high-impedance nodes 0.3 mm / 0.3 mm clearance,
# Power 1.0 mm, HighCurrent 1.5 mm, TankDrive). All rules apply to TRACKS and VIAS only,
# so fixed pad geometry (the LM1875's 1.7 mm pin row, 0805 feedback parts, snubber caps)
# is not flagged; route_board.py hands the router the same numbers as per-class
# clearances. The per-footprint "kp_*" rule areas (no tracks / vias between a part's
# pins or under its body) and the edge / hole keepouts use KiCad's own keepout test.
# On this 4-layer stack every outer trace sits 0.21 mm over a plane, so 0.6 mm of spacing
# couples like ~2 mm did on the two-layer boards; Power<->HiZ separation comes from that
# geometry plus the 0.3 mm class clearance (a wider rule blocked DIP pin access).
# 1. HighCurrent copper (PA_OUT / ZOB / SPK / +33V5 / VRAW, the 24 Vrms AC1 / AC2 secondary)
#    keeps 0.4 mm from every signal trace, high- or low-impedance.
(rule hc_to_signal
  (condition "(A.Type == 'Track' || A.Type == 'Via') && A.NetClass == 'HighCurrent' && (B.NetClass == 'Default' || B.NetClass == 'HiZ')")
  (constraint clearance (min 0.4mm)))
# 2. Reverb tank DRIVE (3 Vrms; class TankDrive = R_DRVO / TKDRV / TANK_IN) keeps 0.6 mm from
#    the tank RETURN path (20 mV): 11 mm parallel runs at -37 dB on the first 2-layer routing.
(rule tank_drive_to_return
  (condition "(A.Type == 'Track' || A.Type == 'Via') && A.NetClass == 'TankDrive' && (B.NetName == 'TANK_OUT' || B.NetName == 'RF2' || B.NetName == 'QRG' || B.NetName == 'WET' || B.NetName == 'DRVP')")
  (constraint clearance (min 0.6mm)))
# 3. (errata #31) The component-side ground POUR keeps 1.0 mm from high-impedance copper
#    (class HiZ: gates, the RF nodes ahead of them, tone ladder and wipers, tank return,
#    LFO timing, MRB tank, the PA + input) -- twice the 0.5 mm it keeps from everything
#    else. Those nodes' capacitance to ground is then the trace over the plane (about
#    1 pF per cm) and nothing the pour adds; kicad/gen/rf_audit.py reports it per net.
#    Top layer only: on the planes a wider opening would merge the openings of
#    neighbouring pins into a slot.
(rule pour_to_hiz
  (layer "F.Cu")
  (condition "A.Type == 'Zone' && B.NetClass == 'HiZ'")
  (constraint clearance (min 1.0mm)))
# 4. JLCPCB: silkscreen text stays 0.15 mm off every pad (their capability table, "Pad
#    To Silkscreen"). Text only: a label that touches a pad loses strokes to the mask
#    opening; a footprint outline that grazes its own pad (the stock 3 mm LED does) is
#    simply clipped by the mask, which the Gerber export subtracts from the silk.
(rule silk_to_pad
  (condition "A.Type == '*Text' && B.Type == 'Pad'")
  (constraint silk_clearance (min 0.15mm)))
